@startuml installation-and-first-run
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

' Installation from zero and the first run of the main loop.
' Sources: main loop spec DRAFT v0 §6, §11.3; curator-playbook process
' configuration DRAFT v3.3 §2.3, §8.1; curator-inference-manager.

title Installation and first run
caption Sources: main loop DRAFT v0 §6, §11.3; process configuration v3.3 §2.3, §8.1

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor $SERVICE
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $SERVICE_LINE
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $COMMITTED
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $COMMITTED_LINE

start
:Install Curator
(script from the website or Homebrew);
:Initialize the root directory from the template package:
Skillfile.json, Playbook.json, keeper.toml, task-board.config.json;
:Install through Curator:
keeper skill with the <i>keeper</i> command,
board, designer and librarian roles (on demand),
base environment profiles;
:Initialize the main loop's board and commit the root;
if (Hardware meets the published minimum?) then (yes)
  :Install an engine package and a small local model
  (curator-inference-manager);
  :Start the main loop on the local model;
  :Questionnaire: which subscriptions and harnesses?
  Add runtime bindings; the person logs in;
else (no)
  :Authenticate a harness fit for
  the root-orchestrator role;
  :Start the main loop on it;
endif
:Offer channels: messengers through waggle providers
(terminal until then: <i>keeper attach</i>);
:Pair the companion app:
QR code, keys exchanged and pinned;
:The person asks; the main loop proposes processes
from published packages; the designer creates one;
:The person confirms on the phone;
:The main loop starts the process's root orchestrator;
stop

@enduml
